{"title":"Cedarline Home","sub":"The chatbot says it handles 35% of customers. Does it?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Retail","geo":"United States","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"AI business case · containment vs resolution · cost per contact","prompt":"Cedarline is a home-furnishings retailer whose service centre handles 2 million customer contacts a year. A vendor proposes an AI chatbot and claims it would save about $3M a year. The head of customer service asks you to check the claim before signing.","clarify":[{"q":"Cost of a contact today?","a":"About $6 for an agent to handle a call or chat."},{"q":"The vendor's claim?","a":"The chatbot fully handles 35% of conversations without passing them to an agent."},{"q":"Chatbot costs?","a":"$0.40 per conversation (every contact would start with the bot) plus $500k a year for the platform."},{"q":"Pilot data?","a":"In a one-month pilot, 20% of customers the bot 'handled' contacted Cedarline again within a week about the same issue."}],"structure":{"root":"Will the chatbot save Cedarline money, and how much?","branches":[{"head":"Contacts avoided","items":["Handled by the bot","Come back later"]},{"head":"Cost of the bot","items":["Per conversation","Platform"]},{"head":"Customer experience","items":["Satisfaction","Which issues suit a bot"]}]},"hypothesis":"'Handled by the bot' isn't the same as 'resolved'. If some customers come back, the saving is smaller than the vendor says.","questions":[{"q":"Recreate the vendor's $3M estimate.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>2M × 35% = 700k contacts avoided × $6 = $4.2M. Less bot costs: 2M × $0.40 + $0.5M = $1.3M. Net: <b>$2.9M</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Now use the pilot data on customers who come back.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.46pt\" height=\"171.36pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.46 171.36\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linej