judge the vendor on resolution (no repeat contact), not containment.</p>"},{"q":"How would you roll it out?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Start with simple, high-volume questions: order tracking, delivery slots, returns policy</li><li>Hand over to an agent quickly for damaged goods and complaints, with the chat history</li> <li>Pay the vendor partly on resolution rate, measured as no repeat contact within 7 days</li><li>Track customer satisfaction for bot and agent contacts separately</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Go ahead, but expect about $2.1M a year of savings, not $3M. The vendor counts every conversation the bot doesn't pass on as a saving, but 20% of those customers come back, so the real saving is about 29% lower. Start with simple order and delivery questions, hand complaints to agents quickly, and tie the vendor's fees to resolution rather than containment. Risk: customer frustration if the bot blocks access to an agent.","great":["Rebuilds the vendor's number","Distinguishes containment from resolution","Revises the saving with pilot data","Designs the rollout around simple contacts"],"id":75,"slug":"cedarline-home"}